On Mar 6, 2:24 pm, masquerade...@gmail.com wrote:
> I've heard mentions in many different places of intentionally avoiding
> fights and decreasing your own level as a strategy. This is a newbie
> question, but what is the advantage of limiting or decreasing your
> level, what classes should do it, and when?


It's almost never a good idea in general.  But I highly recommend
doing the XL1 protection racket (as a pacifist, more or less) a few
times to learn the skills involved--it's not the high percentage play,
but doing it until you're pretty decent at it teaches you a LOT.
After that, you may want to avoid skyrocketing in levels until after
you've bought protection, but I find in practice the considerable
benefits of leveling up at a reasonable pace outweigh the downsides.
If you're getting near buying protection you may want to keep an eye
on the XP until you make your purchase.

More XP, hitting more often, getting more skill slots, extra PW and
spell effects, lower spell failure rates, etc are all very valuable.



